From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:33:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] api/call-link-join: send the group key a join ACK asks for

A call link joined second gets rekey="1" in the link_join ACK's group_info
and in no later group_update. Only the group_update handler fanned the key
out, so neither account ever sent the epoch: maybeStartMedia waited for it
forever and the call stayed silent (no "starting media", 0 frames each way).
The join now runs the same fan-out when its ACK asks for the key.

Validated: engine_call_link_test.go (the fan-out runs once for a rekey=1 ACK
and not without it; fails without the change). Not yet on a live call.
---
 CHANGELOG.md             |  5 +++++
 engine.go                |  3 +++
 engine_call_link_test.go | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 engine_group_api.go      | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

